"""
Binds the clocks of libc through the runtime in lib/prelude.c, which calls clock_gettime.

- It reaches C with @embed, so it is an unsafe module.
- Standard.Time is the safe module built on it, and the one a programme imports.
- The wall clock gives zero when it could not be read.
- The monotonic clock gives a negative number in a build without one; hasMonotonic says which.

    if hasMonotonic() then
        let now: Int64 := monotonicReading();
    end if;
"""
pragma Targets(Names => "linux openbsd freebsd darwin wasm");
module Bindings.Time is
    """
    Nanoseconds since the epoch from the wall clock, or zero when it could
    not be read.
    No contract: a binding to C; the safe module built on it states the contracts.
    """
    function wallNanos(): Nat64;

    """
    Whether this build has a clock that does not go backwards.
    No contract: a binding to C; the safe module built on it states the contracts.
    """
    function hasMonotonic(): Bool;

    """
    Nanoseconds from the monotonic clock, or a negative number when this
    build has none.
    No contract: a binding to C; the safe module built on it states the contracts.
    """
    function monotonicReading(): Int64;
end module.
